{
  "_README": [
    "One representative map point per subsystem, for the DEMO dashboard.",
    "Derived, not surveyed: the centroid of the subsystem's SOURCE members",
    "that have a coordinate in samples/gi_coordinates.json (falling back to",
    "CORE, then any member). Regenerate with scripts alongside that file.",
    "",
    "A centroid is used because every subsystem has SEVERAL sources and",
    "GITETs are shared between subsystems (GITET_NBRJA belongs to both",
    "SS_LBK and SS_BLL), so no single GITET can represent one subsystem.",
    "",
    "'anchor_points' is how many DISTINCT coordinates the centroid averages;",
    "1 means the anchor is really just that one site. Subsystems can sit very",
    "close together (SS_GUCL and SS_SLCG currently resolve to the same point),",
    "so any map must spread overlapping markers rather than draw them raw.",
    "Inherits every caveat in samples/gi_coordinates.json."
  ],
